From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] SPARC64: reset the machine on the client interface "boot"
 service

The client interface "boot" service printed "BOOT" and returned. Solaris
calls it to reboot and, when it returns, stops with "panic - kernel:
prom_reboot: reboot call returned!" (after an install, on reboot(1M) and
init 6). Reset the machine instead; the bootspec isn't kept, the firmware
boots its boot-device.

NOT WORKING YET: "reset-all" at the ok prompt resets the machine, but
Solaris 10's "reboot" ends at "rebooting..." and the VM hangs (no
firmware banner within 900 s); kept as .wip.
---
 forth/system/ciface.fs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/forth/system/ciface.fs b/forth/system/ciface.fs
index 146561a..ba33e18 100644
--- a/forth/system/ciface.fs
+++ b/forth/system/ciface.fs
@@ -262,8 +262,10 @@ external
 \ 6.3.2.5 Control transfer
 \ -------------------------------------------------------------
 
+\ The client asks for a reboot (Solaris' reboot, uadmin): reset the
+\ machine. The bootspec isn't kept, the firmware boots its boot-device.
 : boot ( bootspec -- )
-  ." BOOT"
+  drop reset-all
 ;
 
 : enter ( -- )
